===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete|intransitive}} To be disquieted or confused; to be in commotion.
#* {{RQ:Milton Smectymnuus|passage=some notable sophister lies sweating and '''turmoiling''' under the inevitable and merciless delimmas of Socrates}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|transitive}} To harass with commotion; to disquiet; to worry.
#* {{RQ:Spenser Ireland
|passage=It is her fatal misfortune {{...}} to be thus miserably tossed and '''turmoiled''' with these storms of affliction.}}

